##### Key Computed Properties and Methods:

**Auto-detection logic** (in `created` or `watch`):
```javascript
buildInitialMappings() {
  // For each VAR_* header from Excel, try to find a matching PDF variable
  this.mappings = this.excelVariableHeaders.map(header => {
    const normalizedExcel = header.replace('VAR_', '').toUpperCase().trim();

    // Check saved config first
    if (this.savedConfig && this.savedConfig[header]) {
      return {
        excelHeader: header,
        pdfVariable: this.savedConfig[header],
        autoMatched: false,
      };
    }

    // Auto-detect: find PDF field whose name (stripped of [$...]) matches
    const match = this.availablePdfVariables.find(v => {
      const normalizedPdf = v.name.replace(/\[\$|\]/g, '').toUpperCase().trim();
      return normalizedPdf === normalizedExcel;
    });

    return {
      excelHeader: header,
      pdfVariable: match ? match.name : null,
      autoMatched: !!match,
    };
  });
}
```

**`availablePdfVariables`** (computed):
```javascript
// Flatten all variable-type fields across all PDFs, deduplicated by name
computed: {
  availablePdfVariables() {
    const seen = new Set();
    const vars = [];
    for (const pdfId in this.allPdfFields) {
      for (const field of this.allPdfFields[pdfId]) {
        if (field.type === 'variable' && !seen.has(field.name)) {
          seen.add(field.name);
          vars.push({
            name: field.name,
            displayName: field.name.replace(/\[\$|\]/g, ''),
          });
        }
      }
    }
    return vars;
  },
  unmappedVariables() {
    const mappedNames = new Set(this.mappings.map(m => m.pdfVariable).filter(Boolean));
    return this.availablePdfVariables.filter(v => !mappedNames.has(v.name));
  }
}
```

**`getFieldPreviewValue(field)`**:
```javascript
getFieldPreviewValue(field) {
  // Find the mapping for this field
  const mapping = this.mappings.find(m => m.pdfVariable === field.name);
  if (mapping && this.firstRecordData) {
    const varName = mapping.excelHeader.replace('VAR_', '');
    return this.firstRecordData[varName] || field.exampleText;
  }
  return field.exampleText;  // fallback to example text
}
```

**PDF rendering**: Reuse the same `pdfjs-dist` approach as `view-file.vue`'s preview dialog. Load the Blob, render to canvas, overlay positioned fields.

**Emit events**:
- `@confirm` with `{ mappings, resolvedVariableValues }` -- the confirmed mapping and re-keyed variable values
- `@save-config` with the mapping configuration object
- `@update:modelValue` for v-model dialog toggle

